			<key>candidate</key>
			<string>Pix Aud / Pix Audio</string>
			<key>checkedOn</key>
			<string>2026-08-27</string>
			<key>finding</key>
			<string>Established PIX audio/video recorder coverage makes the intended “pix audio” reading commercially adjacent to professional media equipment. This is not an exact Pixaud mark result, but it compounds the pronunciation and audio-category ambiguity for a player.</string>
			<key>url</key>
			<string>https://www.tvtechnology.com/be-blogs/5571</string>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>candidate</key>
			<string>Canis97 / Canis 97 / Canis-97</string>
			<key>checkedOn</key>
			<string>2026-08-27</string>
			<key>finding</key>
			<string>NASA identifies Sirius as the brightest star in the night sky in the constellation Canis Major. This supports the intended indirect celestial reference, while also confirming that the reference must stay verbal and abstract rather than become dog imagery or provider-adjacent branding.</string>
			<key>url</key>
			<string>https://science.nasa.gov/universe/stars/types/</string>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>candidate</key>
			<string>Canis97</string>
			<key>checkedOn</key>
			<string>2026-08-27</string>
			<key>finding</key>
			<string>Winamp's own community forum records its release in 1997. The “97” component is used solely as a historical software-era allusion; it must not copy Winamp's name, llama mascot, interface, or any other trade dress.</string>
			<key>url</key>
			<string>https://forums.winamp.com/forum/community-center/general-discussions/25720-what-happened-to-amp</string>
		</dict>
